---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Converter from '../components/Converter.astro';

const title = 'Unicode to Preeti Converter — Nepali Text Tools';
const description =
  'Convert Nepali Unicode text to Preeti font encoding in your browser. Handles conjuncts, reph and the i-matra reordering that trips up simple converters.';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebApplication',
  name: 'Unicode to Preeti Converter',
  applicationCategory: 'UtilitiesApplication',
  operatingSystem: 'Any',
  offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
  description,
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} schema={schema}>
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="hangs intro">
      <h1>Unicode to Preeti</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Paste Nepali Unicode and get Preeti-encoded text you can drop into a
        document that still uses the old font.
      </p>
    </div>

    <Converter mode="unicode-to-preeti" sample="नेपाल सरकार, कार्यालयको निर्णय अनुसार वर्ष २०८२" />

    <div class="hangs hangs--thin">
      <h2>Reading the output</h2>
      <p>
        Preeti output looks like scrambled English until the Preeti font is
        applied. That is expected. The font maps Devanagari shapes onto ASCII
        codepoints, so <span class="preeti-text">gd:t]</span> and नमस्ते are the
        same word in two different encodings.
      </p>
      <p>
        To use the result, paste it into your document, select it, and set the
        font to Preeti. If Preeti is not installed on your computer, the text
        will keep showing Latin letters.
      </p>

      <h2>What this converter gets right</h2>
      <p>
        Preeti stores some letters in the order they are drawn rather than the
        order they are spoken, which is where most converters go wrong. Three
        cases matter:
      </p>
      <p>
        The i-matra is drawn to the left of its consonant, so कि is typed
        <span class="preeti-text">ls</span> — the matra first. Reph, the र् that
        rides above a following consonant, is typed after the syllable it sits
        on, so कर्म becomes <span class="preeti-text">sd{'{'}</span>. Conjuncts
        pair a half form with a full one, making क्क into
        <span class="preeti-text">Ss</span>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each of these is covered by tests that convert a word to Preeti and back
        again, checking it survives the trip unchanged.
      </p>

      <h2>Going the other way</h2>
      <p>
        Editing the right pane converts back to Unicode as you type. For longer
        documents, the <a href="/preeti-to-unicode">Preeti to Unicode</a>
        converter gives that direction its own page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .intro {
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
  }
</style>
